% ADJ52 case-16 — patient observations + queries.
% Same vocabulary as rulebook.adj. Observations ONLY for what THIS 81-year-old
% diabetic woman actually has. The skin biopsy was OBTAINED but its result is
% NOT given (the vignette ends at "a skin biopsy was obtained"), so neither
% biopsy(...) value is observed — it is the open uncertainty / next step.

% --- demographics / host ---
observe age(over_50)
observe patient_sex(female)
observe history(diabetes_mellitus)
observe medication(therapeutic_warfarin)

% --- presentation / site ---
observe anatomic_site(lower_leg)
observe history(skin_break_portal_of_entry)
observe symptom(pain_out_of_proportion)
observe symptom(cloudy_nonpurulent_drainage)
observe skin(scattered_papules_and_macules)

% --- course: three antibiotic regimens failed ---
observe course(refractory_to_multiple_antibiotics)

% --- constitutional / labs (discordant with infection) ---
observe vital(afebrile)
observe wbc(normal)
observe ldh(elevated_and_rising)

% --- imaging ---
observe imaging(discrete_intramuscular_lesion)
observe imaging(deep_muscle_infiltration)
observe imaging(regional_lymphadenopathy)
observe imaging(no_gas_in_tissues)

% ===== QUERIES =====
% q1 — unifying underlying diagnosis (each candidate)
? diagnosis(primary_cutaneous_dlbcl_leg_type)
? diagnosis(bacterial_cellulitis)
? diagnosis(anticoagulation_intramuscular_hematoma)
? diagnosis(soft_tissue_sarcoma)
? diagnosis(necrotizing_soft_tissue_infection)

% q3 — recommended next step
? next_step(skin_biopsy_histopathology)
? next_step(continue_broaden_antibiotics)
? next_step(surgical_exploration_fasciotomy)
